  "id": "Compound::DB01037 - Gene::1559",
  "verbalization": "Selegiline exerts its effects through a series of interconnected molecular interactions that ultimately lead to the modulation of Cyp2c9. The evidence suggests that Selegiline causes a condition (Burning In Throat, Unintended Pregnancy, or Prostate Carcinoma) which, in turn, is associated with the binding of specific molecules to Cyp2c9. This indicates a potential mechanism where Selegiline influences the activity of Cyp2c9 via the indirect pathways of its effects on other biological processes. The lowest common ancestors of these relationships—Tertiary Amino Compound, Organic Molecule, and Nitrogen Molecular Entity—highlight a progression from a general molecular class to more specific interactions, suggesting a possible role in the regulation of Cyp2c9 through metabolic or enzymatic pathways. The consistent involvement of Cyp2c9 in these pathways, despite the varied clinical outcomes, underscores the importance of Cyp2c9 in the pharmacological response to Selegiline.",
